<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia's ABA to discuss Internet with EC.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia's ABA to discuss Internet with EC.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Broadcasting Authority (ABA) said on Tuesday it has been invited to present views and findings on regulation of the Internet and on-line services to the European Commission in Brussels, Belgium.</p>
<p>&quot;The ABA welcomes discussion at an international level about the potential for Internet content labelling,&quot; ABA chairman Peter Webb said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;We are keen to explore the possibilities of developing internationally accepted labelling schemes which address the major issues of concern around the world regarding Internet content,&quot; Webb said. -- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
